Phase 2 verification report (FR-2 episode focus)

Commands and outcomes:
- flutter analyze -> No issues found! (ran in 4.1s)
- CI=true flutter test -> 356 passed, 0 failed (baseline 349, +7 new)

Measured D-pad walk on the real SeriesDetailScreen at the device viewport
(1920x1080, density 240, dpr 1.5 -> 1280x720 logical), 3-episode season 1
plus a 2-episode season 2 with no files:

  entry  -> node=FocusableAction              cue=true  "Back"
  down 1 -> node=EpisodeList.chip             cue=true  "S1 3/3"
  down 2 -> node=EpisodeList.row              cue=true  "1 S1E1"
  down 3 -> node=EpisodeList.row              cue=true  "2 S1E2"
  down 4 -> node=EpisodeList.row              cue=true  "3 S1E3"
  down 5 -> node=SeriesDetail.actionBar.first cue=true  "Search All Missing"
  down 6 -> node=SeriesDetail.actionBar.first cue=true  "Search All Missing"
  up     -> walks back up the episodes
  right  -> node=EpisodeList.rowSearch        cue=true
  left   -> node=EpisodeList.row              cue=true  "2 S1E2"

Before this phase the same walk was:
  down 1 -> "S1 7/7"          (chip)
  down 2 -> "Search All Missing"
  down 3..8 -> stuck on "Search All Missing"
so every episode was skipped and none could be selected.

Files changed:
- lib/shared/widgets/media_detail/episode_list.dart: episode rows became real
  focus stops; deterministic D-pad walk owned by the widget; season chip focus
  owned by a FocusableAction wrapper; public EpisodeListState with
  focusFirstChip/focusFirstRow.
- lib/shared/widgets/media_detail/action_bar.dart: firstActionFocusNode and
  explicit left-to-right traversal order.
- lib/features/library/series_detail_screen.dart: anchor that routes Down from
  the header into the list; first-action focus node for the exit; Select now
  plays or searches (no silent no-op for a missing episode).
- test/features/library/episode_focus_test.dart (new): 7 tests.

Three framework findings, each measured rather than assumed:
1. Numeric traversal orders were attached correctly but did not win. Episode
   rows span x 189..1252, so geometry picked the action-bar button nearest the
   row centre, which was 'Delete Series'. The last hop is now delegated to the
   host. An inner FocusTraversalGroup also had to be removed, because it scopes
   traversal to itself.
2. ChoiceChip ignores requestFocus() on an external node (hasPrimaryFocus
   stayed false), so the chip is now the visual only and a FocusableAction owns
   focus.
3. ExcludeFocus sets descendantsAreFocusable: false, which also rejects the
   wrapper's own focus request. Only the chip is excluded.

Why: the owner reported that Down from the season chips skipped the episodes
entirely and landed on the bottom buttons, leaving no episode selectable with
the remote. Delete Series is now unreachable by Down, which removes a
destructive action from a stray Select.
